# Teaching materials part - governed by IEEE LOM (aligned), exportable through Common Cartridge.
# Each deck described as it stands: made for the 1st edition, awaiting renewal by the slide lineage.

<http://example.org/sen0414/materials> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0414: teaching materials"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.46.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414/materials/1.46.0> ; owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414/materials/1.45.0> ;
    dcterms:identifier "sen0414_materials_v1_46_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "Released as 1.14.0 on 2026-09-25: this record had been changed in place across 13 releases (sen0414-v2.10.0 to v2.22.0) while keeping the name v1_0_0; each of those changes added or repointed page entries, so each counts as a MINOR step. Now also names the renamed decks and legacy slides. 1.23.0 adds the chapter 5 deck, RDODI document and page, and corrects the version this record states inside itself: the files named v1_20_0 and v1_21_0 still said 1.19.0. 1.24.0 points the chapter 5 page at version 9.9 (SPARQL samples load on selection, formatted agent answers, an on-request question builder covering every concept). 1.25.0 points the pages of chapters 1 to 5 at version 9.10 (the chapter 5 page adds a written question bank and a live-model question), the decks of chapters 1 to 4 at their repaired files, and the page ABoxes of chapters 1 to 4 at new files. 1.26.0 adds the chapter 6 deck, RDODI document and page, and points the chapter 5 page at version 9.11. 1.27.0 points the pages of chapters 1 to 4 at version 9.11 (each with a written question bank of 61, 54, 69 and 74 items) and their page ABoxes at new files. 1.28.0 points the pages of chapters 1 to 6 at version 9.12 (clickable references, a page-wide search, a check on the local model's replies) and their page ABoxes at new files. 1.29.0 points the pages of chapters 1 to 6 at version 9.13 (progress, a review queue, section links, notes, a cheat sheet, marks on answers, code exercises) and their page ABoxes at new files. 1.30.0 points the pages of chapters 1 to 6 at version 9.14 (ten question types with corrections, mock midterm and final exams from a code, a choice of live model) and their page ABoxes at new files. 1.31.0 corrects three statements this record made about itself. The pages of chapters 1 to 5 are repointed from version 9.14 to the version 9.24 files that are on disk, and the chapter 6 page from version 9.14 to its own 9.19 file, so a query asking where this chapter's page is no longer answers with a file ten versions old. The five renewed decks are repointed at their current files, including the chapter 1, 2 and 3 decks reworked as lectures. The chapter 5 deck and page are recorded as serving the course outcome LO-6, which the approved outcomes ontology sources to chapter 5 of the 3rd edition and which this record had not carried; and every chapter page now names its own deck through dcterms:relation, so the deck that sits beside it is reachable from the register rather than from nowhere. No vocabulary term is added or removed. | 1.37.0 (2026-10-08): the five chapter pages repointed to version 9.27.0 - the two-fold look-and-feel (CME materials standard 1.0.0) with the story layer, the Learn sections, concept map, ontology-graph layers, chapter ERD, fit, reading area, relocate on every diagram and the narrative diagrams typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping, ported from the proven template series onto this course's line (templates 9.26.0-9.37.0); the entries had still named 9.24.0 while the released pages were 9.26.0. | 1.38.0 (2026-10-12): adds chapter 12 of the 3rd edition, Designing and Deploying Command Line Programs - its lecture deck, RDODI document and interactive page 9.28.0 - built on the owner's instruction of 2026-10-11, which lifts for this chapter the scope exclusion recorded in the slide lineage (ex:Excl_CommandLine, ruling of 2026-09-24). The chapters 7 to 11 renewed since 1.37.0 are not yet entered here; their entries are left for a register update of their own rather than written from this chapter's run. The page configuration (course_page_config_v1_4_0.json) still embeds 1.37.0 in every page's corpus; this version is the register of record and is embedded once a configuration names it. | 1.39.0 (2026-10-12): fills the gap 1.38.0 named: adds the chapters 7 to 11 renewed since 1.37.0 - Dictionaries and Structuring Data, Manipulating Strings, Text Pattern Matching with Regular Expressions, Reading and Writing Files, and Organizing Files - each with its lecture deck, RDODI document and interactive page 9.28.0, read from disk rather than from any prior summary. Each deck's dcterms:replaces was checked against the 1st-edition deck list by chapter title and only entered where a real correspondence was found (chapters 7-11 all have one, chapters 5 of the 1st edition through 9); cme:servesOutcome was drawn only from the outcomes ontology's own per-chapter sourcing (01-outcomes/sen0414_outcomes_v1_0_0.ttl), not from any chapter's test_config course_lo field, which was found on inspection to hold the same fixed canary value and question in every chapter 1-11 and so is not a per-chapter signal; on that basis chapter 8 and 9 serve LO-2 and chapters 10 and 11 serve LO-5, while chapter 7 serves no outcome specifically named for it and carries none. Two of the five chapters' shipped .docx files were found to have gone stale against their own renewed .ttl (chapter 10, unchanged since a pre-renewal draft under the same version number) or to be missing for the renewed version entirely (chapters 8, 9 and 11); all four were regenerated from their current .ttl by the course's own converter (08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_docx_v1_0_0.py) before this version was written, so every docx this version names actually matches its ttl. All five decks were independently re-run through deck_check under Python 3.14.6 in this session (0 mismatches on every one) rather than trusted from their build commits alone. | 1.40.0 (2026-10-12): adds chapter 13 of the 3rd edition, Web Scraping - its RDODI document (the research package: document, research record, domain TBox, ABox and SHACL shapes, all at 1.0.3) and its interactive page 9.28.0. The package is entered at 1.0.3, not at the 1.0.2 of the research commit: the page test re-runs every stored input-output example in the page's in-browser Python (CPython 3.13.2) and found three that differ there from CPython 3.14.6 (the urllib user-agent version, robotparser's wildcard rule, webbrowser.BaseBrowser), so 1.0.3 rewrites those three examples to give the same result in both (chapter 12's precedent, its 1.0.1 and 1.0.2); the document, TBox and SHACL shapes are otherwise identical to 1.0.2, the ABox differs in those three examples only, and the research record in its verification stamp, and the 1.0.2 files stay on disk. The page serves the course outcome LO-7 (collect information from the web by fetching and parsing pages and by automating a browser), whose source in the approved outcomes ontology is chapter 13 of the 3rd edition. The chapter 13 lecture deck is not entered here: it is being built in a separate session, which registers it. The page configuration (course_page_config_v1_6_0.json) now embeds this version in every page's corpus, and the page-data builder (sen0414_page_data_v2_9_0.py) names that configuration; both are new files, since the builder holds the configuration's filename as a constant. Nothing else in this record changed. | 1.41.0 (2026-10-12): points the chapter 13 page at its rebuild 9.28.1 (same template 9.42.0; the page file is a new name because 9.28.0 was already committed): it adds the Lecture tab from the chapter 13 deck's slide titles and notes and shows the deck's own five worked examples (title, url, status, robots, soup) in the Lab, so the page and the slides carry the same code. The deck is still not entered here. | 1.42.0 (2026-10-12): adds the chapter 13 lecture deck (26 slides, recorded under Python 3.14.6), which serves LO-7 and replaces the 1st-edition Chapter11WebScraping_YA deck (Deck_02, the web scraping chapter of that edition), and relates the chapter 13 page to it; the page is entered at its rebuild 9.28.2, which embeds this register. | 1.43.0 (2026-10-12): adds the chapter 14 lecture deck (26 slides, recorded under Python 3.14.6), which serves LO-3 and replaces the 1st-edition Chapter12WorkingWithExcelSpreadheets_YA deck (Deck_03), and adds the chapter 14 RDODI document and interactive page, entered at version 9.29 (page template 9.43.0, which embeds the openpyxl and et_xmlfile wheels because the browser's Python has no openpyxl); the page relates to the deck and embeds this register. | 1.44.0 (2026-10-12): adds the chapter 15 lecture deck (26 slides, built under Python 3.14.6 with Google never reached; it states on each slide that shows stand-in or fixture output that it does, and marks four slides NOT EXECUTED), the chapter 15 RDODI document and the chapter 15 interactive page, entered at version 9.30 (page template 9.44.0, which embeds the ezsheets, google-api-python-client and dependency wheels so that the examples run in the browser against the study's stand-in for Google); the page relates to the deck and embeds this register. No approved outcome names chapter 15 as a source, so neither the deck nor the page is entered as serving one. | 1.45.0 (2026-10-12): adds the chapter 16 lecture deck (26 slides, built under Python 3.14.6 with SQLite 3.53.1; its single-run timings are labelled as such and slide 23, the graphical database tools, is marked NOT EXECUTED), the chapter 16 RDODI document and the chapter 16 interactive page, entered at version 9.31 (page template 9.45.0). The page runs its examples in the browser's Python 3.13.2 with SQLite 3.39.0 and says where that differs from the recorded Python 3.14.6 and SQLite 3.53.1 results; the page relates to the deck and embeds this register. No approved outcome names chapter 16 as a source, so neither the deck nor the page is entered as serving one. | 1.46.0 (2026-10-12): adds the chapter 17 lecture deck (26 slides, built under Python 3.14.6 with pypdf 6.20.1 and python-docx 1.2.0; slides 8 and 23 are marked NOT EXECUTED and the one time it shows, slide 16, is labelled a single measured run), the chapter 17 RDODI document and the chapter 17 interactive page, entered at version 9.32 (page template 9.46.0, which unpacks the pypdf and python-docx wheels the page embeds so that the examples run in the browser). The page relates to the deck and embeds this register. No approved outcome names chapter 17 as a source, so neither the deck nor the page is entered as serving one."@en .

