# Renewed for the 3rd edition by the SEN0414 slide lineage.
sen0414:Deck_Ch01_3e a schema:LearningResource ; dcterms:title "Chapter 1: Python Basics - renewed for the 3rd edition" ;
    dcterms:format "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation" ;
    cme:fileInPart "03-materials/ch01/SEN0414_Ch01_PythonBasics_3e_v3_0_0.pptx" ;
    cme:renewalStatus "Redesigned for the classroom on 2026-10-06 to the CME materials look-and-feel standard v1.0.0 - the same warm-ivory theme the SEN0401 chapter decks carry, drawn by the shared renderer 08-tooling/deck_render_v1_0_0.js with the course's own >>> chip: 23 numbered slides with an agenda of exact slide ranges, a summary before the live-linked resources, and a takeaway strip on every content slide. Three dated, sourced 5N1K stories carry WHO/WHERE/WHEN/READ fact rows with live links: Python's 1989 Christmas birth at CWI (Guido van Rossum's portrait, Daniel Stroud, CC BY-SA 4.0, credit on-slide), the textbook's free online edition the course pins, and PEP 703 free-threading - whose gil console reads sys._is_gil_enabled() from the interpreter in front of the class. Every console is labelled, syntax-coloured with fonts computed so no line wraps, and shown WITH its executed result - TypeErrors and NameErrors exactly as Python raised them; environment rows are environment-truth, re-executed on the build machine (examples_out_v1_2_0.json) so the version tuple on the slide is what the interpreter actually answered. deck_check_v1_0_1.py re-ran 63 examples off the finished file with 0 mismatches and the layout check found no overflowing frame; the resources slide links only sources the chapter's own checked sources file records. Licences in 03-materials/ch01/assets/ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md; the review cycle in 08-tooling/ch01-deck/REVIEW_v3_0_0.md; earlier versions are in git history (the structure discipline keeps one active version per stem)." ;
    dcterms:replaces sen0414:Deck_07 ; cme:servesOutcome sen0414:LO1, sen0414:LO4 ;
    dcterms:source "03-materials/ch01/rdodi/sen0414_ch01_research_v1_0_1.ttl; 08-tooling/sen0414_ch01_stories_v1_0_0.py (self-checked); 08-tooling/ch01-deck/examples_out_v1_2_0.json; 08-tooling/ch01-deck/sources_out_v1_0_0.json" .
