sen0414:Deck_Ch03_3e a schema:LearningResource ; dcterms:title "Chapter 3: Loops - renewed for the 3rd edition" ;
    dcterms:format "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation" ;
    cme:fileInPart "03-materials/ch03/SEN0414_Ch03_Loops_3e_v3_0_0.pptx" ;
    cme:renewalStatus "Redesigned for the classroom on 2026-10-06 to the CME materials look-and-feel standard v1.0.0 (shared renderer, the >>> chip): 21 numbered warm-ivory slides with an agenda of exact slide ranges, a summary before the live-linked resources, and a takeaway strip on every content slide. Three dated, sourced 5N1K stories carry fact rows with live links and licensed portraits: the Gauss schoolroom sum - honestly labelled as a legend traced to the 1856 memorial - settled either way by the chapter program (the loop and the closed form both answer 5050); Dijkstra's handwritten EWD831 of 1982-08-11 under range's half-open rule; and the Mersenne Twister (Matsumoto and Nishimura, 1997-98, period 2^19937-1) inside import random. while-vs-for is taught as two WHOLE programs printing the same transcript; eight program panels are captioned name-and-lines and verified by program_check_v2_0_0.py (verbatim slices, transcripts re-executed with recorded inputs), 58 console rows re-run by deck_check_v1_0_1.py, 0 mismatches; the whole recording was first re-executed on the build interpreter (examples_out_v2_1_0.json). Width and height gates keep code from wrapping, a pre-build audit sizes every panel from the recording, and the layout check found no overflowing frame. Licences in 03-materials/ch03/assets/ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md; the review cycle in 08-tooling/ch03-deck/REVIEW_v4_0_0.md; earlier versions are in git history." ;
    dcterms:relation sen0414:Deck_08 ; dcterms:source "03-materials/ch03/rdodi/sen0414_ch03_research_v1_0_0.ttl" .
