    cme:renewalStatus "Redesigned for the classroom on 2026-10-06 to the CME materials look-and-feel standard v1.0.0 (shared renderer, the >>> chip), completing the first five chapters of both courses on one look: 23 numbered warm-ivory slides, agenda with exact ranges, summary before the live-linked resources, takeaway strips throughout. Three dated, sourced 5N1K stories with fact rows, live links and licensed pictures: the Harvard Mark II moth of 1947-09-09 (the Navy's own logbook photograph, public domain, the file title's 1945 mislabel honestly noted on the provenance), Kernighan's 1979 judiciously-placed-print-statements sentence (his Bell Labs photo, CC BY 2.0), and PEP 282's 2002 birth of the logging module. Fourteen whole programs with transcripts carry the chapter - a real crash read bottom-up, unwinding and 3.11 add_note, asserts with and without messages plus the -O caveat RUN rather than recited, logging levels/file/force/disable all executed, the factorial bug found by its log on one slide and fixed on the next, and the seeded coin toss whose types confess with BOTH recorded runs on the slide - each panel captioned name-and-lines and verified by program_check_v2_0_1.py (verbatim slices; transcripts re-executed with recorded inputs), deck_check re-running the console rows; recording and checks under an installed Python 3.14.6; 0 mismatches; the layout check found no overflowing frame. Licences in 03-materials/ch05/assets/ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md; the review cycle in 08-tooling/ch05-deck/REVIEW_v2_0_0.md; earlier versions are in git history." ;
