    cme:renewalStatus "Built on 2026-10-11 at the CME standard following the chapter 1-7 pattern: a 25-slide lecture deck over a document TTL rewritten twice in the same run (1.1.0 for the fresh multi-paragraph prose per section, then 1.1.1 adding two cross-section references that connect two previously isolated ERD entities). Four web-sourced 5N1K stories, 0 self-check failures ('The encoding written on a diner placemat', 'Nine companies agree on one table of characters', 'One proposal, created in a single day, gave Python its f-string', 'The clipboard the chapter's programs use is fifty years old'); no photographs embedded - Wikimedia Commons returned a sustained HTTP 429 from the build session's egress IP, documented in stories_img_v1_0_0.json rather than faked or substituted. Six narrative diagrams, all passing grounding. Re-verified in this session under Python 3.14.6: deck_check found 74 console rows with 0 mismatches. test_config bumped to 1.2.0 to carry the corpus_kinds/course_outcomes/code_layers overrides every other chapter's config already had. The chapter's own build ran the full Playwright suite twice against page 9.28.0: 382/382 passing, 0 failures, 0 skipped. The 1st edition covered this material in its chapter 6, so this deck renews sen0414:Deck_12. Its renewed document had shipped with no matching .docx at all (only the original v1.0.0 draft existed on disk); a genuine sen0414_ch08_document_v1_1_1.docx was generated today (2026-10-12) from the current ttl by the course's own converter (08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_docx_v1_0_0.py), so Doc_Ch08 below now names a docx that actually matches its ttl." ;
