    cme:renewalStatus "Built on 2026-10-11 at the CME standard: the document TTL rewritten with fresh multi-paragraph prose over the existing TBox/ABox (63 sections, 39 cross-concept mentions, no isolated subject). Four dated, sourced 5N1K stories, no photographs (Wikimedia Commons still 429-rate-limited): Kleene's 1951 regular events, Thompson's 1968 NFA construction, Perl's 1987 birth, and Secret Labs' 1999 sre module. Six narrative diagrams, grounding >= 0.8 on every one. Executed corpus of three whole programs (contactExtractor, strongPasswordDetector, regexStrip) and the 22-slide lecture deck's own examples. Re-verified in this session under Python 3.14.6: deck_check found 60 console rows with 0 mismatches. test_config 1.0.2 deliberately names LO-1 rather than LO-2 for its own course-question canary, because LO-2's own wording is this chapter's vocabulary almost verbatim - a test-fixture choice, not evidence against this register's own cme:servesOutcome below, which instead follows the outcomes ontology's own sourcing. The chapter's own build ran page 9.28.0 clean: 190/190 features, 63/63 widgets, 0 failures. The 1st edition covered this material in its chapter 7, so this deck renews sen0414:Deck_13. Its renewed document had shipped with no matching .docx; a genuine sen0414_ch09_document_v1_0_1.docx was generated today (2026-10-12) from the current ttl by the same converter." ;
