    cme:fileInPart "08-tooling/ch10-deck/sen0414_ch10_deck_v1_0_0.pptx" ;
    cme:renewalStatus "Built on 2026-10-11 at the CME standard: the document TTL rewritten with fresh multi-paragraph, cross-referenced prose over the existing TBox/ABox (59 concepts, 93 relations - 54 stated, 39 co-mentions - no isolated subject). Four dated, sourced 5N1K stories, no photographs (Wikimedia Commons still 429-rate-limited): Pitrou's 2012 pathlib (PEP 428), Thompson and Pike's 1992 UTF-8 diner placemat, Thompson's 1979 dbm, and Crockford and Morningstar's 2001 JSON write-up. Six narrative diagrams, grounding >= 0.8 on every one. Executed corpus of three whole programs (capitalsQuiz, madLibs, regexSearchFiles) and the 24-slide lecture deck's own examples. Re-verified in this session under Python 3.14.6: deck_check found 85 console rows with 0 mismatches. One content-ordering fix made during the original build: Path joining and Path flavours were swapped in document order after the page's own semantic passage search ranked 'Path flavours' one place outside its top-8 window for the single word 'flavours'. test_config 1.0.1 sets bank_complete false (chapter 10 ships no question bank) and deliberately names LO-1 rather than LO-5 for its own course-question canary, because LO-5's own wording - path objects, walking folder trees - is this chapter's vocabulary almost verbatim; this register's cme:servesOutcome below instead follows the outcomes ontology's own sourcing. The chapter's own build ran page 9.28.0 clean, twice: 188/188 features, 59/59 widgets, 0 failures each run. The 1st edition covered this material in its chapter 8, so this deck renews sen0414:Deck_14. Its shipped document_v1_0_1.docx had gone stale against this rewrite - the blob was unchanged since an earlier, pre-CME-standard draft under the same version number and never regenerated when the ttl was rewritten; a fresh, genuinely matching sen0414_ch10_document_v1_0_1.docx was generated today (2026-10-12) from the current ttl by the course's own converter, replacing the stale file." ;
