    cme:fileInPart "08-tooling/ch11-deck/sen0414_ch11_deck_v1_0_0.pptx" ;
    cme:renewalStatus "Built on 2026-10-11 at the CME standard: the document TTL rewritten with fresh multi-paragraph, cross-referenced prose over the existing TBox/ABox (64 concepts, 126 relations - 58 stated, 68 co-mentions - every level-2 section has an outgoing mention). Four dated, sourced 5N1K stories, no photographs (Wikimedia Commons still 429-rate-limited): Katz and Conway's 1989 public-domain ZIP release, Gailly and Adler's 1995 zlib, Kare's 1983 Macintosh trash-can icon, and Daley and Neumann's 1965 Multics tree-structured file system. Six narrative diagrams, grounding >= 0.8 on every one. Executed corpus of three whole programs (backupProject, selectiveCopy, dateRenaming) and the 23-slide lecture deck's own examples. Re-verified in this session under Python 3.14.6: deck_check found 101 console rows with 0 mismatches (under the sandbox's default 3.13.16 the same deck shows two further AttributeErrors on Path.copy/Path.move, pathlib additions new to 3.14 - an interpreter-version artefact, not a content defect). One fact correction made during the original build: shutil.move onto an existing destination FILE of the same name was found to silently overwrite it (os.rename under the module's own docstring), not raise shutil.Error as the prior research record described; shutil.Error is raised only when the destination is a FOLDER already holding an item of the source's name - corrected across the document, ABox and deck and verified directly against Python 3.14.6. test_config 1.0.1 sets bank_complete true (the chapter's existing 106-item question bank covers all 64 concepts and re-passes question_bank_check against the rewritten document) and deliberately names LO-1 rather than LO-5 for its own course-question canary, for the same reason as chapter 10; this register's cme:servesOutcome below instead follows the outcomes ontology's own sourcing. The chapter's own build ran page 9.28.0 clean, twice: 189/189 features, 64/64 widgets, 0 failures each run (378/378 checks overall). The 1st edition covered this material in its chapter 9, so this deck renews sen0414:Deck_15. Its shipped document_v1_0_0.docx predated this rewrite entirely; a genuine sen0414_ch11_document_v1_0_1.docx was generated today (2026-10-12) from the current ttl by the course's own converter." ;
